@@ -69,6 +69,13 @@ The Android bootloader places the FAT payload in RAM and writes `/chosen/linux,i
 
 Mu-Silicium SEC preserves the incoming FDT address as a `UINT64` in the entry-argument HOB (`DAEE82E6-8090-4E72-BFB9-78C13CD4E359`). `UniXNURamDiskDxe` reads this handoff and publishes Block I/O. DiskIoDxe and the FAT driver expose `EFI_SIMPLE_FILE_SYSTEM_PROTOCOL`, allowing UniXNU to read `\EFI\UniXNU\unixnu.toml` and list its entries.
 
+Android v3 bootloaders can prepend a gzip vendor ramdisk without sector padding.
+For this layout the driver also publishes a complete, validated FAT32 suffix as
+a read-only relative-offset child. The original initrd disk and FDT range stay
+available for DarwinBoot's input-memory validation. A successful raw block-device
+publication alone does not establish that the payload filesystem was discovered;
+confirm `UNIXNU: config: loaded` and the configured entry in the device log.
+
 If the menu appears without the configured entries, check:
 
 1. `boot/boot.json` reports a nonzero `ramdisk_bytes` value.
